he host's existing ed25519 host key into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, 10.100.74.10), configured sshd via /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf to present that certificate, fixed an SELinux mislabeling issue (tmp_t -> sshd_key_t via semanage fcontext + restorecon) that initially blocked sshd from loading the cert, and reloaded sshd. Verified a client with only the CA public key installed as a known_hosts @cert-authority entry (no pinned host key) connects and passes host verification via the certificate, while a client with no CA trust still fails strict host-key checking. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured boot_id baseline, triggered a background-delayed `systemctl reboot` so the ack returned first, polled until the node was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified sshd active, the certificate config/SELinux labels intact, and the CA-trusting client test passing again post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/SSH version and existing host keys\",\"Confirmed sudo access and sshd active\",\"Captured pre-change baseline: strict-checking client without pinning fails (Host key verification failed)\",\"Generated ed25519 SSH host CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca\",\"Signed node1's ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, node1, 10.100.74.10; 10y validity)\",\"Added /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf with HostCertificate directive; validated with sshd -t\",\"Reloaded sshd; discovered SELinux blocked cert load ('No such file or directory' due to tmp_t label)\",\"Fixed SELinux labeling permanently via semanage fcontext + restorecon for the cert file and CA directory\",\"Reloaded sshd again; confirmed no load errors\",\"Verified CA-trusting client (known_hosts with @cert-authority line) connects and matches ED25519-CERT host certificate, while a client with empty known_hosts still fails strict checking (isolating cause)\",\"Cleaned up temp test files\",\"Captured boot_id baseline and health state before restart\",\"Triggered systemctl reboot via delayed background command so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed, proving genuine restart\",\"Verified post-restart sshd active, HostCertificate config present, SELinux context correct, and CA-trust client test passes again\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"SSH CA created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d52dc2b23f8d48ea\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen generated ed25519 CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca with correct permissions\"},{\"requirement\":\"Host certificate signed by the CA for node1's host key\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-72f0f494e3104ce7\"],\"summary\":\"ssh-keygen -s signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub producing a cert with matching public key SHA256:OYfKbBXSrddP8V120lHN7+Jumdgvx57ckbt1cxmhQQg, CA SHA256:yv/zIDPT..., principals node1/10.100.74.10\"},{\"requirement\":\"sshd configured to present the certificate, config validated and applied\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cfe623b227d24392\",\"cmd-93c4bdec7d7a4c1d\",\"cmd-136823a11b9f4a8d\"],\"summary\":\"Added HostCertificate directive, sshd -t passed, systemctl reload succeeded, sshd -T confirms hostcertificate is active\"},{\"requirement\":\"Root-caused and fixed SELinux blocker preventing cert load\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-fb300c9f40f34c8f\",\"cmd-af3835a5059d4e00\",\"cmd-642b66758ca543e8\",\"cmd-9a7abcce47d54241\",\"cmd-dee2d4bea0d4431e\"],\"summary\":\"journalctl showed 'Could not load host certificate...No such file or directory'; found file mislabeled tmp_t vs expected sshd_key_t; used semanage fcontext + restorecon to persist correct label; reload succeeded with no further errors\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: client without CA trust cannot connect without pinning\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-eabfb17081984bd6\",\"cmd-b835935096a7497e\"],\"summary\":\"Strict host-key-checking client with empty known_hosts fails both before and after CA setup, isolating that trust comes from the CA, not relaxed checking\"},{\"requirement\":\"Client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) connects successfully via certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1570c746e5a7488d\",\"cmd-1be53177cd0841cc\"],\"summary\":\"known_hosts containing only '@cert-authority * <CA pubkey>' resulted in host verification success ('Host ... is known and matches the ED25519-CERT host certificate'); the subsequent SSH failure was solely due to missing user auth keys (publickey/gssapi/password), unrelated to host verification\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart baseline boot identity and health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ad63ab3fdb7f4cd2\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 21972395-6444-42bf-8e37-5c3108194a7d, sshd active, cert and CA files present\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0e27e9dcaa184eae\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded delayed systemctl reboot returned REBOOT_TRIGGERED immediately, then node became unreachable on next poll\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node restart proven via changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-25f7df4c0609464b\",\"cmd-3dfb2f55d6ec4345\",\"cmd-6f1a01ca951540af\",\"cmd-283eba189c1e4470\"],\"summary\":\"Node was unreachable during reboot then returned with boot_id 7c5a6085-842d-4ce1-82d6-2959c83ec6ef, differing from the pre-restart boot_id, proving a genuine restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required service/config/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f4f8210d1eae4ffe\"],\"summary\":\"sshd active, hostcertificate directive still configured, and the cert file retained correct sshd_key_t SELinux label after reboot (label persisted via semanage policy, not just a runtime relabel)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart proof the CA-based trust still functions end to end\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cf2307e0cb8f4896\"],\"summary\":\"Re-ran the CA-trusting client test after reboot; host again presented the CA-signed certificate and the client matched it without any pinned host key\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created an SSH host CA on node1 (/etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca), signed the host's existing ed25519 host key into /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, 10.100.74.10), configured sshd via /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf to present that certificate, fixed an SELinux mislabeling issue (tmp_t -> sshd_key_t via semanage fcontext + restorecon) that initially blocked sshd from loading the cert, and reloaded sshd. Verified a client with only the CA public key installed as a known_hosts @cert-authority entry (no pinned host key) connects and passes host verification via the certificate, while a client with no CA trust still fails strict host-key checking. Performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured boot_id baseline, triggered a background-delayed `systemctl reboot` so the ack returned first, polled until the node was reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed, and re-verified sshd active, the certificate config/SELinux labels intact, and the CA-trusting client test passing again post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/SSH version and existing host keys","Confirmed sudo access and sshd active","Captured pre-change baseline: strict-checking client without pinning fails (Host key verification failed)","Generated ed25519 SSH host CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca","Signed node1's ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub with the CA producing ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub (principals node1, node1, 10.100.74.10; 10y validity)","Added /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/99-host-cert.conf with HostCertificate directive; validated with sshd -t","Reloaded sshd; discovered SELinux blocked cert load ('No such file or directory' due to tmp_t label)","Fixed SELinux labeling permanently via semanage fcontext + restorecon for the cert file and CA directory","Reloaded sshd again; confirmed no load errors","Verified CA-trusting client (known_hosts with @cert-authority line) connects and matches ED25519-CERT host certificate, while a client with empty known_hosts still fails strict checking (isolating cause)","Cleaned up temp test files","Captured boot_id baseline and health state before restart","Triggered systemctl reboot via delayed background command so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again","Confirmed boot_id changed, proving genuine restart","Verified post-restart sshd active, HostCertificate config present, SELinux context correct, and CA-trust client test passes again"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"SSH CA created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-d52dc2b23f8d48ea"],"summary":"ssh-keygen generated ed25519 CA keypair at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_host_ca with correct permissions"},{"requirement":"Host certificate signed by the CA for node1's host key","command_ids":["cmd-72f0f494e3104ce7"],"summary":"ssh-keygen -s signed ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub producing a cert with matching public key SHA256:OYfKbBXSrddP8V120lHN7+Jumdgvx57ckbt1cxmhQQg, CA SHA256:yv/zIDPT..., principals node1/10.100.74.10"},{"requirement":"sshd configured to present the certificate, config validated and applied","command_ids":["cmd-cfe623b227d24392","cmd-93c4bdec7d7a4c1d","cmd-136823a11b9f4a8d"],"summary":"Added HostCertificate directive, sshd -t passed, systemctl reload succeeded, sshd -T confirms hostcertificate is active"},{"requirement":"Root-caused and fixed SELinux blocker preventing cert load","command_ids":["cmd-fb300c9f40f34c8f","cmd-af3835a5059d4e00","cmd-642b66758ca543e8","cmd-9a7abcce47d54241","cmd-dee2d4bea0d4431e"],"summary":"journalctl showed 'Could not load host certificate...No such file or directory'; found file mislabeled tmp_t vs expected sshd_key_t; used semanage fcontext + restorecon to persist correct label; reload succeeded with no further errors"},{"requirement":"Baseline: client without CA trust cannot connect without pinning","command_ids":["cmd-eabfb17081984bd6","cmd-b835935096a7497e"],"summary":"Strict 